{"name":"Nightfall in Suburbia","hex":"#0011dd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nightfall","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The close of the day; the coming of night.","Nocturnal emission."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nightfall"},{"term":"suburbia","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The suburbs as a whole and all that characterizes or pertains to them;  the suburbs as encapsulated or represented by the typical characteristics or qualities of the people living there, especially complacency, conformity, conservativeness, dullness, etc. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suburbia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Suburb","blocks":[{"text":"A suburb is an area within a metropolitan area which is predominantly residential and within commuting distance of a large city. Suburbs can have their own political or legal jurisdictions, especially in the United States, but this is not always the case, especially in the United Kingdom, where most suburbs are located within the administrative boundaries of cities. In most English-speaking countries, suburban areas are defined in contrast to central city or inner city areas, but in Australian English and South African English, suburb has become largely synonymous with what is called a \"neighborhood\" in the U.S. Due in part to historical trends such as white flight, some suburbs in the United States have a higher population and higher incomes than their nearby inner cities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hempstead%2C_Manhasset%2C_and_Little_Neck_bays.jpg/330px-Hempstead%2C_Manhasset%2C_and_Little_Neck_bays.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suburb","wikidata":"Q188509"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Belmont_Court%2C_Monroe%2C_NJ_08831.jpg/500px-Belmont_Court%2C_Monroe%2C_NJ_08831.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Belmont_Court%2C_Monroe%2C_NJ_08831.jpg/500px-Belmont_Court%2C_Monroe%2C_NJ_08831.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABelmont_Court%2C_Monroe%2C_NJ_08831.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/View_over_Griffith_NSW_1.jpg/500px-View_over_Griffith_NSW_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/View_over_Griffith_NSW_1.jpg/1280px-View_over_Griffith_NSW_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/View_over_Griffith_NSW_1.jpg/500px-View_over_Griffith_NSW_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Suburban housing in the regional city of Griffith, New South Wales in Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AView_over_Griffith_NSW_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/United_States_Suburb_Image.jpg/500px-United_States_Suburb_Image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/United_States_Suburb_Image.jpg/1280px-United_States_Suburb_Image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/United_States_Suburb_Image.jpg/500px-United_States_Suburb_Image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Suburban areas in the United States. Bellevue, Washington (top left) Orchard Park, New York (top right) Fremont, California (bottom left), and Dulles, Virginia (bottom right)","link":"https:/